this video was posted this week on wall  street bets  a reddit forum dedicated to discussing  stock and options trading  this little rocket represents gme the  stock ticker for video game retailer  gamestop  for weeks users of the subreddit have  been encouraging each other to scoop up  shares  and make bullish wagers on the stock in  less than a month  gme rose from under twenty dollars a  share to well over three hundred dollars  on some days  before falling on thursday after brokers  placed restrictions on  trading wall street has been totally  stunned by what's happened with gamestop  this has basically never happened before  alexander osiepovic  covers futures and stock exchanges for  the wall street journal and has explored  the forces behind gamestop's dramatic  swings  gamestop has become a battleground  between small investors who are banding  together on  online forums like reddit and  professional investors  who are shorting the stock or betting  that will fall here's what's going on  with gamestop  wall street bets is one of the most  popular forums on reddit  it's a place where people get together  share trading ideas and go after  particular stocks in a kind of  coordinated fashion  they can cause a big run-up in that  stock's price in recent weeks  investors on wall street bets have  targeted gamestop's short sellers  who saw the company as overpriced and  were betting the shares would fall  the wall street bets crowd was buying up  shares and betting the opposite  causing the stock to go on a wild ride  behind that is  a couple of things one of them is  momentum trading  that's when people chase games they see  a stock is going up they buy more of it  because they'll  likely keep going up but while the rise  might have appeared to be as simple as  average investors  buying shares and pumping up the price  it also had to do  with options options are contracts that  allow investors to buy  or sell a stock at a specified price  either on  or until a specified date it has gotten  a lot easier and cheaper for people to  trade options over the past few years  now the world is your trading floor  commissions have come down  and brokers have invested a lot of time  and effort into making  easy to use interfaces to allow people  to buy and sell them and even do complex  strategies  options trading volumes set a record  last year averaging just under 30  million contracts a day  this year that number is over 40 million  options come in two forms put options  confer the right to sell shares under  specified terms  and call options confer the right to buy  them  many of the wall street's bets users  were buying call options to bet that the  price would rise  look at the market on tuesday january  26th for example  gamestop closed at just under 148  dollars  at that moment call options to buy  gamestop shares at 200  a piece by friday were trading at just  19. a share  if gamestop rallied the price of the  options might have risen  and call holders would have been able to  sell these options for a quick profit  the question is why were the shares  surging when much of the action was in  options it's because when an investor  buys a call option  someone else has to sell it to them  typically an electronic trading firm  that buys and sells stocks  when they sell the investor the call  option they often hedge their bet  by purchasing shares of the stock in  question  gamestop options trading volumes  exploded during the past two weeks  especially for call options which drove  brokers to buy  more of the stock driving it up even  further  this dynamic isn't just playing out with  gamestop traders at wall street bets  moved on to amc blackberry and nokia as  well  amid soaring shares on january 28th  popular online brokerages  including robinhood and interactive  brokers group restricted access  to trading high-flying stocks including  game stop  shares plunged trading a stock like  gamestop in a situation like this is  extremely risky  if you are dupe playing with this stuff  you are playing with fire  it's unclear if the authorities have any  means reigning the sin  wall street bets users called foul some  pledging to find other ways to  participate in the market  regardless of the chaos it causes
 

